{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# Phase 2 COMPLETE — fix pushed as Gerrit change 1980\n\nCommit `c9c9a41591`, branch `fix-naga-snapshot` off `origin/main`.\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1980\n\n## Fix\n\n**AC-1 — a review no longer writes a full copy.** New `src/rebar/_snapshot/delta_tree.py`\n(301 LOC): pick the newest published `tickets-<sha2>` entry whose commit this clone can read,\nhardlink the paths the two trees share, and let `git checkout-index --force -z --stdin` rewrite\nonly the paths that differ. `materialize_tickets` gains ~10 lines of wiring; the pre-existing\n`_materialize_tree` call is now the fail-closed fallback and is otherwise untouched.\n\nApproach chosen against ADR 0005's integrity guarantee, as the AC asks. The two rejected\nalternatives are rejected for cause, not preference:\n\n* *Pin a coarser/stabler key* would re-open bug 2a6f — `ae6f2ac57a` moved the pin to the live\n  tracker HEAD precisely because a staler pin made the verifier report recorded comments as\n  nonexistent. Trading freshness for size would regress a fixed bug.\n* *Materialize only the paths the gate reads* is not knowable ahead of time: the agent may\n  `show_ticket` any ticket in the store.\n\nHardlinking changes only **storage**, never contents — `tickets-<sha>` still holds exactly the\ntree at `<sha>` — so the attestation basis is untouched. That is asserted, not assumed: the\noracle checks every entry's path set against `git ls-tree -r` and every file's bytes against\n`git show`.\n\n**AC-3 — byte accounting.** Already satisfied by `itchy-arbored-peccary` and deliberately not\nre-implemented. It did need a correction to stay *true*: `entry_size` summed `st_size` per file\nwith no inode awareness, so shared blobs would have been counted once per referencing entry and\ninflated `byte_total` by a factor of k. It now charges `st_size // st_nlink`, which sums back to\nthe true on-disk size across the k links, leaves unshared files (`st_nlink == 1`, i.e. every\ncode entry) completely unaffected, and is self-correcting under eviction.\n\n**AC-4 — docs.** ADR 0005 D2 now states the key-reuse assumption explicitly (\"an immutable key\nis not automatically a good one\") and records how each entry kind satisfies it — code entries by\n*key* reuse, ticket entries by *content* reuse. `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` gains the\noperator-facing version.\n\n## AC-2 — RED -> GREEN, held out, with teeth\n\nThe oracle was authored before any fix existed, confirmed RED for the right reason, then moved\n**out of the worktree entirely** (not merely omitted from the prompt) with `tests/` declared\noff-limits to the implementing subagent. It asserts the algorithmic property — distinct-inode\nbytes per resolution — never wall-clock.\n\n    RED   4 adjacent-SHA resolutions consumed 3200027 bytes; one tree is ~800000   (4.00x)\n    GREEN 1 passed\n\n**Mutation 1** — disable the donor path, re-introducing the confirmed mechanism: RED again at\n*exactly* 3200027 bytes. Restored: GREEN.\n\n**Mutation 2, and why it exists.** Reviewing my own oracle I found it could not catch the\nfailure mode that mattered most. An implementation that enumerated donor contents by *walking\nthe donor directory* instead of by `git ls-tree` passes every assertion on a clean fixture — and\nin production would either copy untracked files into an entry whose tree does not contain them,\nor (with a count-based completeness check) fall back on every single call, leaving the fix\npermanently inert while CI stayed green. An independent write-safety audit had just measured\n**4,844 `.cache.json` files inside one live entry**, so this is the normal state of a donor, not\nan edge case.\n\nSo `test_donor_untracked_files_do_not_leak_into_a_new_entry` seeds a donor with exactly those\nartefacts. Against the walk-based implementation it fails on\n`tickets/..cache.json.abc.tmp` leaking into the new entry; against the shipped one it passes.\n\n**Refactoring litmus.** Every assertion is on observable on-disk output — distinct-inode bytes,\ninode identity, path sets vs `git ls-tree`, contents vs `git show`. No private name, no\nintermediate variable, no source grep. Demonstrated rather than claimed: a `ruff format` pass\n(behaviour-preserving) kept it green while the behavioural mutation still turned it red.\n\nOne defect of my own surfaced during validation — an unused local that tripped `make lint`. It\nchanges no assertion, and both the suite and mutation 2 were re-run after removing it.\n\n## Two safety findings that changed the design\n\nBoth came from the independent audit, and both would have been silent failures:\n\n1. **Donor contents != donor tree** (above). Corrected mid-implementation.\n2. **`.ticket-write.lock` is a *tracked* file**, so it is materialized into every entry — and\n   `fcntl.flock` is scoped to the **inode**. Hardlinking it would make a lock taken through\n   entry A block a writer in entry B, invisibly, until it deadlocked. It is now forced into the\n   rewrite set and never shared.\n\nSymlinks and gitlinks also fail closed (`os.link` would dereference a symlink; a gitlink has no\nblob), as do an absent-objects clone, an incomplete donor, a cross-device or hardlink-less\nfilesystem, and a delta no smaller than the tree.\n\n## Gates\n\n`make lint` PASS - `make typecheck` PASS (614 files) - complexity `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`\n(no baseline edit) - **full unit sweep 11,939 passed, 44 skipped** - targeted snapshot/gate\nsuites 116 passed - `check_raw_git_writes`, `check_wall_clock_asserts`, `check_comment_hygiene`,\n`check_config_reads`, `check_config_ownership`, `check_server_manifest`,\n`check_verify_gate_parity`, `check_adr_numbers`, `check_docs_index` all PASS.\nModule sizes: `repo_snapshot.py` 739, `delta_tree.py` 301 — both inside the 800 cap, and the new\nmodule is well clear of the 100-LOC floor.\n\n## Scope\n\nNothing hand-deleted from the live store, as instructed. Neither sibling ticket was absorbed:\n`undamaged-epidermic-kakarikis` (janitor starts only in the review-bot process) and\n`famous-digital-dingo` (no mtime bump on a cache hit) both survive this change untouched — this\nis production-side only, it reclaims nothing and adds no `touch_entry`.\n\nThree tickets filed and linked `discovered_from`: `atrophied-exact-indianabat` (entries are not\nactually immutable; this already breaks the reverify TOFU digest), `adroit-degraded-gourami`\n(the code-entry path has the identical construct — measured at 4.00x — held out because code\nsnapshots are the attestation basis for signed verdicts and deserve their own review), and\n`subtle-brinish-fugu` (the dead `_cleanup` field).\n\nNo description edit — evidence in comments to keep any attestation current."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787296827378806001,"uuid":"dbf75093-0f9e-4428-855b-89f40124189e"}